===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[abdomen]] (especially a fat one).
#: {{ux|en|You've grown a '''belly''' over Christmas! Time to join the gym again.}}
# {{tcl|en|stomach|id=Q1029907}}
#: {{ux|en|My '''belly''' was full of wine.}}
# {{tcl|en|uterus|id=Q9612}}
#: {{syn|en|matrix<qq:now archaic>|metra|uterus|womb}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Jeremiah|1|5|passage=Before I formed thee in the '''bellie''', I knew thee; {{...}}}}
# The lower [[fuselage]] of an [[airplane]].
#* {{RQ:Mandela Long Walk to Freedom|year=2010|page=454|passage=There was no heat, and we shivered in the '''belly''' of the plane.}}
# The part of anything which resembles (either closely or abstractly) the human belly in protuberance or in concavity; often, the {{l|en|fundus#Noun}} (innermost part).
#: {{co|en|the '''belly''' of a flask, muscle, violin, sail, or ship}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Jonah|2|2|passage={{...}} I cried by reason of mine affliction vnto the Lord, and hee heard mee; out of the '''belly''' of hell cried I, and thou heardest my voyce.}}
#* {{RQ:Stevenson Treasure Island|text=At last I got my knife and cut the halyards. The peak dropped instantly, a great '''belly''' of loose canvas floated broad upon the water {{...}} }}
## {{senseid|en|of a knife}} The main curved portion of a knife {{l|en|blade#Noun}}.
## {{lb|en|architecture}} The hollow part of a curved or bent {{l|en|timber#Noun}}, the convex part of which is the [[back]].

====Usage notes====
* Formerly, all the splanchnic or visceral cavities were called bellies: the lower belly being the abdomen; the middle belly, the thorax; and the upper belly, the head.

